+
+## Owned workspace initialization
+
+An ordinary caller-owned directory can initialize without a standing WRITE_OWNER grant. Initialization borrows a non-inheriting owner right while holding the directory open, applies the required Low label, and restores the final capability DACL without that borrowed right. Explicit label-write denies and reparse-point bootstrap targets are refused. Failed initialization restores the original label and DACL or reports restoration failures; it never starts an unrestricted child.
+
+Existing ordinary owned descendants are provisioned through pinned native object handles. Reparse points, multiply linked files, protected DACLs, other owners and explicit non-Low labels are not broadened. Per-object query/set avoids Win32 automatic inheritance touching outside links; capability revocation visits the same ordinary objects. Temporary owner access never inherits and rolls back on failure.
