+## Complete resources
+
+download reuses the text fetcher’s URL, public-address, proxy, redirect and cancellation policy. Binary responses are returned only in full; both declared and streamed byte-limit overflow reject instead of returning a truncated file.
+
+Anonymous cross-origin public redirects are allowed with fresh route/address validation at every hop. Private literals, credentialed URLs, non-HTTP schemes, HTTPS downgrades and excess hops remain blocked. Results retain origin/route/proxy-origin/status observations; transport failures retain bounded machine error codes without copying credential-bearing messages.
